    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The Visayas region faced a major power shortfall after a machine everyone depends on failed. The equipment failure, compounded by ongoing shutdowns at other plants and high summer demand that strained the system, left over 950 megawatts unavailable. In response, authorities mandated power cuts to prevent a bigger outage, leaving ordinary people to deal with rolling blackouts.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "why-1",
          "why-2",
          "how-2",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "center": "result-0",
        "channel": "toned",
        "channel_role": "toned",
        "composition_mode": "ADR-0008"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "As a major power plant component, the broken link in the chain was Unit 2. When it tripped offline, the grid operator—everyday workers keeping the lights on—had to declare an emergency for the Visayas region. The system couldn't handle everyone needing power at once, so they had to cut power to keep a critical transmission line from overloading, resulting in a huge loss for ordinary people.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
